Track 1: First One To Touch The Sun-Dial Loses
- Story & Context: Out in the salt flats of Ouarzazate, two young traders bypassed the thermal regulators on a salvaged Roland SH-101 and routed its voltage through a hollow eucalyptus trunk to see whose lungs would collapse first. The resulting feedback loop accidentally harmonized with the midday heat, causing an entire oasis encampment to drop their water jugs and dance uncontrollably for six hours. The incident proved that the machine's cold logic could be broken by human breath, birthing the very first Sandmotorik rhythm. As the solar battery finally bubbled and melted into the sand, Oumou shouted across the salt pan, "Keep the air moving or the sky falls down!"
