Track 3: The Great Dune That Swallowed Brother Kinski
- Story & Context: Legend speaks of an eccentric European organist who wandered off into the Grand Erg Oriental carrying nothing but a Farfisa organ and a bottle of peppermint schnapps, never to be seen again. Decades later, the Caravanserai discovered his instrument half-buried in a dune, its keys bleached white and perfectly tuned by desert wind. They rigged the organ to a three-meter didgeridoo and played a sun-drenched eulogy that echoed across three countries, transforming a local ghost story into an eternal anthem of freedom. As the sun set red over the ridge, the crowd sang into the wind, "He didn't perish, he just became the bass!"
